{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And if he is poor.</b> That his means do not reach to give this valuation." "<b>And he shall stand him.</b> The one whose valuation is being assessed — before the priest, and he shall assess him according to the means of the one making the valuation." "<b>According as his hand reaches.</b> According to what he has, he arranges it, and leaves him enough for his livelihood: a bed, a bolster and a cushion, and tools of his trade; if he was a donkey-driver, he leaves him his donkey (Bava Metzia 114; Arakhin 23)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:54.668019614Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}